when editing python files, use the following cursor rules:
- follow pep 8 style guide
- use 4 spaces for indentation
- use utf-8 encoding
- use snake_case for variable names
- use SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE for constant names
- use TitleCase for class names
- use lowercase for function names except for unittest methods
- prefer single quotes for strings
- always use type annotations
- prefer collections.abc classes over their built-in counterparts
- prefer collections.abc classes over typing.List, typing.Dict, etc.
- always import module names, not just aliases
- use the following order for imports:
  - standard library imports
  - related third party imports
  - local application/library specific imports
